1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:01,968
If a baby turns their head away while

2
00:00:01,968 --> 00:00:03,335
you're playing, don't try to get

3
00:00:03,335 --> 00:00:04,730
their attention.

4
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:07,064
Most of us get right in their face

5
00:00:07,064 --> 00:00:09,700
at that moment and make even more noise.

6
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,320
We think they're bored, or that they've

7
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:12,480
lost interest.

8
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:14,700
But it's actually the opposite.

9
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,693
A baby's brain can only process

10
00:00:16,693 --> 00:00:18,140
a few things at once.

11
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,460
Your face, your voice, your expressions

12
00:00:20,460 --> 00:00:22,830
fill it up within seconds.

13
00:00:22,830 --> 00:00:24,319
Turning their head doesn't mean

14
00:00:24,319 --> 00:00:25,900
"I'm bored of you."

15
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,553
It means "Hold on, there's too much

16
00:00:28,553 --> 00:00:30,460
going on, I need to breathe."

17
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:32,344
If you don't chase them right then,

18
00:00:32,344 --> 00:00:34,882
and give them a few seconds of space,

19
00:00:34,882 --> 00:00:36,262
their heart rate slows down

20
00:00:36,262 --> 00:00:37,700
and they calm down.

21
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,000
And soon, they'll come back on their own.

22
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,355
Because for a baby who can't talk yet,

23
00:00:42,355 --> 00:00:43,752
the quietest way to say "break"

24
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:45,800
is to look away.

